                            <comment id="17097906" author="zjffdu" created="Sat, 2 May 2020 10:42:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Might be related with css, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=Hsuan+Lee&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;Hsuan Lee&quot;&gt;Hsuan Lee&lt;/a&gt;&#160;Do we have any changes in css in 0.9 ?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17097941" author="alexott" created="Sat, 2 May 2020 12:10:42 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Ok, it&apos;s something wrong with my local setup - when I compile 0.9.0-preview1 version, then I get it mangled. When I take version from site, then everything is good. I need to find what is wrong with my setup...&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17097995" author="alexott" created="Sat, 2 May 2020 15:29:09 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;If I replace interpreter in 0.9.0-preview1 with a new version, then everything works just fine...&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13001891/13001891_%D0%A1%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%BE%D0%BA+%D1%8D%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B0+2020-05-02+%D0%B2+16.21.35.png&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But when I use my compiled copy, I get following broken HTML, and error that doesn&apos;t exist in 0.9.0-preview1&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13001892/13001892_%D0%A1%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%BE%D0%BA+%D1%8D%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B0+2020-05-02+%D0%B2+16.10.45.png&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17106017" author="zjffdu" created="Wed, 13 May 2020 06:47:40 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=alexott&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;alexott&quot;&gt;alexott&lt;/a&gt;&#160;Any update on this ?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17106019" author="alexott" created="Wed, 13 May 2020 06:51:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=zjffdu&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;zjffdu&quot;&gt;zjffdu&lt;/a&gt; not really - I tried to do a clean build, removing all caches for npm, etc., but still getting this garbage.&lt;br/&gt;
Unfortunately I didn&apos;t have time for very deep investigation, but at least I have a workaround now - I can just copy interpreter into 0.9 preview release, and everything works correctly - I suspect that some of the JS components could be blocked in my network, or something like.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17161061" author="alexott" created="Mon, 20 Jul 2020 09:19:35 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The reason for that &amp;amp; other things that tags, like, &lt;tt&gt;&amp;lt;i ... /&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;&amp;lt;div .../&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt;, are stopped to work...&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
